invariant: INV-45
file: sha3.c
catches: sha3_equiv_test
reason: block_xor's eight-byte step counts lanes from the block's first
  byte when the block is partly filled, so the bytes go into the wrong
  lanes. A one-call digest starts every block at byte zero and stays
  right; the split absorbs of the SHAKE streams differ.

--- old
        lane[(pos + i) / 8] ^= lane_from_bytes(in + i);
--- new
        lane[i / 8] ^= lane_from_bytes(in + i);
